course: dictionary
lesson: 4737
title: Fun words and real science
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A horoscope is a short prediction about someone's life and future. It is based on where the stars and planets were when that person was born. Each star sign has its own horoscope, and they are often printed in magazines.
explain: The sentence «make a wish on a shooting star, read your horoscope for fun, and still know which is astronomy» gives you clues. The words «for fun» show that people read horoscopes to enjoy them, not as science. The words «still know which is astronomy» tell you that astronomy is the real science of stars and planets.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide what a word means. Ask yourself: what does the sentence want me to notice? Here it wants you to see the difference between a fun story and a true science fact.
fact: A horoscope is a short prediction about your life and future.
fact: A horoscope is based on the position of the stars and planets when you were born.
fact: Horoscopes are often printed in magazines, with one for each star sign.
fact: «Astronomy» is the science of stars and planets. «Astrology» is the belief behind horoscopes.
fact: There is no evidence that horoscopes predict the future, so they are not science.
exercise: «Read your horoscope for fun, and still know which is astronomy.» What is a horoscope? | *A short prediction about your life, based on the stars and planets when you were born | A map of the night sky for astronomers | A kind of rocket that flies into space | A telescope for looking at the Moon
exercise: «Fortune tellers and horoscopes use general statements that fit almost anyone.» What does general mean here? | Only for soldiers in the army | Based on a map of the stars | Very loud | *Not specific, so it could fit almost anyone
exercise: Is a horoscope science? | Yes, scientists have proved it | *No, it is for fun, and there is no evidence it predicts the future | Only if it is printed in a science magazine | Yes, it is astronomy
test: What is the difference between astronomy and astrology? | Astronomy is the study of stars and planets, and astrology is about horoscopes and is not science | They are two names for the same thing | Astronomy is about horoscopes, and astrology is the study of stars | *Astronomy is the science of stars and planets, and astrology is the belief behind horoscopes
test: Where would you usually find a horoscope? | In a space rocket | In a telescope | In a science textbook about the Sun | *In a magazine, with one for each star sign
exam: Read: «There is no evidence they predict the future.» Why should a scientist doubt a horoscope? | Because it is printed in magazines | Because the stars are too far away to see | *Because there is no evidence that it predicts the future | Because it is too long to read
